192	- Check Docker installation
193	- Pull the latest Docker image 
194	- Prompt you to select folders for mounting
195	- Configure Claude Desktop automatically
196	- Restart Claude if possible
197	
198	#### How Docker Persistence Works
199	Desktop Commander creates a persistent work environment that remembers everything between sessions:
200	- **Your development tools**: Any software you install (Node.js, Python, databases, etc.) stays installed
201	- **Your configurations**: Git settings, SSH keys, shell preferences, and other personal configs are preserved  
202	- **Your work files**: Projects and files in the workspace area persist across restarts
203	- **Package caches**: Downloaded packages and dependencies are cached for faster future installs
204	
205	Think of it like having your own dedicated development computer that never loses your setup, but runs safely isolated from your main system.
206	
207	#### Manual Docker Configuration
208	
209	If you prefer manual setup, add this to your claude_desktop_config.json:
210	
211	**Basic setup (no file access):**
