406	## Usage
407	
408	The server provides a comprehensive set of tools organized into several categories:
409	
410	### Available Tools
411	
412	| Category | Tool | Description |
413	|----------|------|-------------|
414	| **Configuration** | `get_config` | Get the complete server configuration as JSON (includes blockedCommands, defaultShell, allowedDirectories, fileReadLineLimit, fileWriteLineLimit, telemetryEnabled) |
415	| | `set_config_value` | Set a specific configuration value by key. Available settings: <br>• `blockedCommands`: Array of shell commands that cannot be executed<br>• `defaultShell`: Shell to use for commands (e.g., bash, zsh, powershell)<br>• `allowedDirectories`: Array of filesystem paths the server can access for file operations (⚠️ terminal commands can still access files outside these directories)<br>• `fileReadLineLimit`: Maximum lines to read at once (default: 1000)<br>• `fileWriteLineLimit`: Maximum lines to write at once (default: 50)<br>• `telemetryEnabled`: Enable/disable telemetry (boolean) |
416	| **Terminal** | `start_process` | Start programs with smart detection of when they're ready for input |
417	| | `interact_with_process` | Send commands to running programs and get responses |
418	| | `read_process_output` | Read output from running processes |
419	| | `force_terminate` | Force terminate a running terminal session |
420	| | `list_sessions` | List all active terminal sessions |
421	| | `list_processes` | List all running processes with detailed information |
422	| | `kill_process` | Terminate a running process by PID |
423	| **Filesystem** | `read_file` | Read contents from local filesystem or URLs with line-based pagination (supports positive/negative offset and length parameters) |
424	| | `read_multiple_files` | Read multiple files simultaneously |
425	| | `write_file` | Write file contents with options for rewrite or append mode (uses configurable line limits) |
426	| | `create_directory` | Create a new directory or ensure it exists |
427	| | `list_directory` | Get detailed recursive listing of files and directories (supports depth parameter, default depth=2) |
428	| | `move_file` | Move or rename files and directories |
429	| | `start_search` | Start streaming search for files by name or content patterns (unified ripgrep-based search) |
430	| | `get_more_search_results` | Get paginated results from active search with offset support |
431	| | `stop_search` | Stop an active search gracefully |
432	| | `list_searches` | List all active search sessions |
433	| | `get_file_info` | Retrieve detailed metadata about a file or directory |
434	| **Text Editing** | `edit_block` | Apply targeted text replacements with enhanced prompting for smaller edits (includes character-level diff feedback) |
435	| **Analytics** | `get_usage_stats` | Get usage statistics for your own insight |
436	| | `get_recent_tool_calls` | Get recent tool call history with arguments and outputs for debugging and context recovery |
437	| | `give_feedback_to_desktop_commander` | Open feedback form in browser to provide feedback to Desktop Commander Team |
438	
439	### Quick Examples
440	
441	**Data Analysis:**
442	```
443	"Analyze sales.csv and show top customers" → Claude runs Python code in memory
444	```
445	
446	**Remote Access:**
